  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Solo Whist. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Solo Whist (or simply 'Solo') is a British trick-taking card game derived from Whist but incorporating bidding elements from Boston and Quadrille. Unlike Partnership Whist, players bid individually to achieve specific goals, such as making 5, 9, or 13 tricks alone ('Solo', 'Abundance', 'Abundance Declared') or losing every trick ('Misere'). It is a game of high skill and nerve.",
    objective: 'Win your bid: in Prop and Cop make 8 tricks with your partner (turned suit as trump); in Solo make 5 tricks alone in the turned suit; in Misère lose every trick (no trumps); in Abundance make 9 tricks alone (you choose trump); in Abundance Declared make all 13 tricks (no trumps, you lead). Settle in units after each deal.',
    gameplay: "Deal 13 cards each; last card to dealer is turned for prospective trump. Bid in order from dealer's left: Prop, Cop, Solo, Misère, Abundance, Abundance in Trumps, Misère Ouverte, Abundance Declared. Higher bid wins; bidding continues until three players pass. If all pass or Prop finds no Cop, redeal. Play: player to dealer's left leads (except Abundance Declared when bidder leads). Follow suit if possible; highest trump wins the trick, else highest card of the led suit. Winner of each trick leads to the next.",
    keyRules: [
      'Follow suit if you can; otherwise play any card.',
      'Highest trump in the trick wins; if no trump, highest card of the led suit wins.',
      'Prop and Cop: two players try to make 8 tricks with turned suit as trump.',
      'Solo: one player tries to make 5 tricks alone. Misère: one player tries to lose every trick.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: true,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Four players, each ultimately playing for themselves, though they form temporary alliances (one against three or two against two) for each hand.',
      deck: 'A standard 52-card pack is used; cards in each suit rank from high to low: A K Q J 10 9 8 7 6 5 4 3 2.',
      equipment: 'A standard 52-card pack is used; cards in each suit rank from high to low: A K Q J 10 9 8 7 6 5 4 3 2.',
      dealing: 'Deal 13 cards each in packets of three until four cards remain, then deal the last four singly; the last card (to the dealer) is turned face up to indicate prospective trump. Dealer may pick it up after the first trick if not played.',
    },
    turnFlow: "Deal 13 cards each; last card to dealer is turned for prospective trump. Bid in order from dealer's left: Prop, Cop, Solo, Misère, Abundance, Abundance in Trumps, Misère Ouverte, Abundance Declared. Higher bid wins; bidding continues until three players pass. If all pass or Prop finds no Cop, redeal. Play: player to dealer's left leads (except Abundance Declared when bidder leads). Follow suit if possible; highest trump wins the trick, else highest card of the led suit. Winner of each trick leads to the next.",
